    <h2>What's this?</h2>

    <p>
        The Spankscuary Webring is a hand-built neighbourhood for spanking stories,
        art, history, humour, blogs, archives, and community. It connects independently
        owned sites so readers can move from one to another without relying on search
        engines, social media feeds, or recommendation algorithms.
    </p>

    <p>
        <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Webring">Webrings</a> are an
        <a href="https://brisray.com/web/webring-history.htm">old idea</a>
        we're bringing back because they still solve a useful problem. Each member
        site participates in the ring, making it possible to discover other sites
        through people rather than platforms. There are good reasons
        <a href="https://www.base31.org/blog/bringing-back-the-webring">webrings and blogrolls are making a comeback</a>:
        human curation, direct connections between independent sites, and the chance
        to stumble onto interesting things an algorithm might never show you.
    </p>

    <h2>How to join</h2>

    <p>
        Spankscuary is for independently maintained sites with substantial
        spanking-related content. Personal sites, blogs, story archives, art sites,
        history projects, forums, and other community resources are all welcome to apply.
        Professional and commercial sites offering spanking-related goods, services,
        writing, art, video, or other work are welcome to apply too.
    </p>

    <p>
        To join Spankscuary, your site needs to be able to participate in the ring
        itself. That means displaying the Spankscuary navigation banner, or another
        approved version of the Previous, Random, and Next links, somewhere readers
        can reasonably find it.
    </p>

    <p>
        A link to the Spankscuary homepage by itself isn't enough. The point of a
        webring is that readers can keep moving around the circle.
    </p>

    <p>
        Want to join? Just
        <a href="https://mijasroom.net/contact/">email Mija</a>
        with the name and URL of your site. I'm the person currently tending
        Spankscuary and adding new member sites. If your site has an RSS or Atom
        feed and you know the address, send that too. If you don't know what an
        RSS feed is, don't worry about it. I can probably find it for you.
    </p>

    <p>
        If you're comfortable with GitHub and would rather do it yourself, you can
        also <a href="{{ meta.repo }}/compare">open a pull request</a>
        with the name and URL of your site and, if available, its RSS or Atom feed.
    </p>

    <p>
        When your site has been added to Spankscuary, I'll let you know and send
        you the banner code to add to your site.
    </p>

    <p>
        Before joining, please also have a look at the
        <a href="/code-of-conduct">Code of Conduct</a>. It's there to help keep
        Spankscuary a welcoming, useful neighbourhood rather than to make joining
        complicated.
    </p>

