    <h3>WordPress</h3>

    <p>
        Once you've received confirmation that your site has been added to the
        Spankscuary member list, decide where you'd like the banner to appear.
    </p>

    <p>
        In WordPress, edit the page, sidebar, footer, or widget area where you'd like
        the banner to appear. Add a
        <code class="ui-label">&lt;Custom HTML&gt;</code>
        block or widget, then paste in the banner code shown above.
    </p>

    <p>
        Save or update the page, then test
        <code class="ui-label">&lt;Previous&gt;</code>,
        <code class="ui-label">&lt;Random&gt;</code>, and
        <code class="ui-label">&lt;Next&gt;</code>.
        The banner identifies your site automatically, so you don't need to edit
        the links when new members join the ring.
    </p>

    <p>
        Put it somewhere readers can find it. A sidebar or footer is a good choice,
        but the bottom of a homepage works too.
    </p>

    <h3>Blogger</h3>

    <p>
        Once you've received confirmation that your site has been added to the
        Spankscuary member list, decide where you'd like the banner to appear.
    </p>

    <p>
        In Blogger, open your blog dashboard and choose
        <code class="ui-label">&lt;Layout&gt;</code>.
        In the sidebar, footer, or other area where you'd like the banner to appear,
        click <code class="ui-label">&lt;Add a Gadget&gt;</code>, then choose
        <code class="ui-label">&lt;HTML/JavaScript&gt;</code>.
    </p>

    <p>
        Leave the title blank unless you'd like to give the gadget a title. Paste
        the Spankscuary banner code shown above into the
        <code class="ui-label">&lt;Content&gt;</code> box, then save it.
    </p>

    <p>
        You can move the gadget to another part of the page by dragging it in the
        <code class="ui-label">&lt;Layout&gt;</code> screen. Put it somewhere readers
        can reasonably find it.
    </p>

    <p>
        Visit your blog and test
        <code class="ui-label">&lt;Previous&gt;</code>,
        <code class="ui-label">&lt;Random&gt;</code>, and
        <code class="ui-label">&lt;Next&gt;</code>.
        The banner identifies your site automatically, so you don't need to edit
        the links when new members join the ring.
    </p>

    <p>
        If the banner doesn't display correctly,
        <a href="https://mijasroom.net/contact/">email Mija</a>
        and I'll help figure it out.
    </p>

